Die Rote Fahne prints the slogan across its front page: the enemy is in Essen and the enemy is in Berlin. It is a correct line, and it satisfies nobody who is actually hungry: the miners want to know who will pay their wages next week. Under occupation the party's district in the Ruhr now works between French patrols and German police.

